copper, zinc, molybdenum, phosphorus, cadmium, and arsenic.
Against the background of the use of a complex feed additive, a
significant increase in magnesium, manganese, nickel, lithium was
noted. Further, the experimental diet increased the rate of various
minerals which stimulate the various enzymatic processes and led
to the beginning of egg-laying 7-12 days earlier in quail laying

